[1626.935198, "o", "== 4. a user pays for a question; the payment is split among owners\r\n"]
[1665.489274, "o", "paid 0.01 NEAR  tx 9wob9cNkerY5xb2B6GT4UF1scKqn5TrjCsWNPgWzAM7L\r\nLaing distal myopathy is caused by mutations in the DMD gene, which provides instructions for making dystrophin, an important protein that helps provide structural support within muscle cells (sarcoplasmic reticulum). Mutations in this gene result in the production of an abnormally short or nonfunctional version of dystrophin. Without functional dystrophin to help maintain the structure of muscle cells, muscles weaken and begin to break down over time. The severity of the resulting muscle weakness depends on the length of the deleted portion of the DMD gene and the number of mutation copies a\r\n"]
